hived_by":null},{"id":279098111,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgxMTE=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:rendering","name":"topic:rendering","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":2666708289,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNjY2NzA4Mjg5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:3d","name":"topic:3d","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":1,"created_at":"2025-05-23T19:50:48Z","updated_at":"2025-05-24T15:41:57Z","closed_at":"2025-05-24T14:15:15Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nv4.4.1.stable.official [49a5bc7b6]\n\n### System information\n\nWindows 11 - Vulkan 1.4.303\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen using the compatibility renderer and adding a Directional light to a properly setup scene (scene has a correctly setup world environment) and then changing the directional light cull mask to ignore a certain render layer from a mesh, the directional light just ignores the cull mask and lights the mesh anyway.\n\nThis appears to only happen with directional lights on the compatibility renderer. Spot and omni lights cull masks work in any renderer and directional light cull mask work in mobile and forward+ renderer.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n- Create a new project in compatibility renderer\n- Create a 3D scene\n- Add a WorldEnvironment with default Environment\n- Add a Sphere 3D mesh and set it to render layer 1\n- Add a Directional light 3D to the scene and position it so it should light the sphere\n- Turn off Ligh > Cull mask layer 1\n\n**What should happen**\n\nThe sphere is no longer lit by the directional light\n\n**What happens instead**\n\nIn the compatibility renderer, the sphere is still lit by the directional light. Changing the renderer to mobile or forward+ fixes the issue\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nProject in compatibility renderer with scene already set up\n\nhttps://github.com/Dancovich/compatibility-lighting-bug","closed_by":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106760/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106760/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"duplicate","pinned_comment":null}